WEBVTT

00:39.610 --> 00:41.240
T-This is so spectacular.

00:41.260 --> 00:42.660
I truly didn't expect it.

00:48.320 --> 00:49.530
Ten years...

00:51.210 --> 00:53.940
I've finally gotten into
the Southern Archives.

00:54.600 --> 00:55.400
Ten years.

00:57.810 --> 01:00.180
What exactly

01:01.340 --> 01:03.390
does the Southern Archives do?

01:04.250 --> 01:05.280
The Southern Archives

01:05.280 --> 01:06.580
collects records of
all the strange and mysterious events

01:06.580 --> 01:08.850
that occur throughout
the southern regions of our country.

01:08.850 --> 01:10.039
It's a secret organization

01:10.039 --> 01:12.300
under the Maritime Supervisory Office.

01:12.990 --> 01:14.850
At least, that's what I believed.

01:15.770 --> 01:17.930
Maritime Supervisory Office?

01:19.060 --> 01:20.670
You really are a cop.

01:21.430 --> 01:23.240
Cousin, I've been so good to you,

01:23.260 --> 01:24.990
and you still don't believe me?

01:25.539 --> 01:27.300
It's because you've been too good to me,

01:27.300 --> 01:28.120
and I trusted you like an idiot.

01:28.120 --> 01:30.280
Look at my neck, my face, and my hand.

01:30.840 --> 01:31.860
Alright, just tell me

01:31.860 --> 01:33.990
what we're looking for. I'll help you.

01:35.250 --> 01:36.460
No destroying anything, though.

01:36.460 --> 01:37.460
I'm watching you.

01:39.090 --> 01:40.009
Right now, we need to find

01:40.009 --> 01:41.410
something very special.

01:42.340 --> 01:43.789
Something special?

01:53.140 --> 01:55.200
Everything's arranged so randomly.

02:05.710 --> 02:06.980
Did you find anything?

02:08.100 --> 02:08.940
No!

02:13.250 --> 02:14.310
[Name: Zhang Hairu] [Name: Zhang Haimo]

02:14.340 --> 02:15.220
[Name: Zhang Haimo]
[Case: Jiulong River Shipwreck Incident]

02:15.240 --> 02:17.000
[Name: Zhang Hailou]
[Case: Panhua Reef Case]

02:17.000 --> 02:19.350
[Note: Risk of exposing
the Southern Archives.]

02:26.000 --> 02:28.780
I mean, has this place...

02:29.630 --> 02:31.190
ever really been in operation?

02:31.190 --> 02:32.850
What kind of question is that?

02:33.190 --> 02:34.630
With this many archives,

02:35.150 --> 02:37.470
if they weren't organized
according to some system,

02:37.470 --> 02:39.530
the place couldn't possibly operate.

02:39.530 --> 02:41.780
Unless someone has a photographic memory,

02:41.780 --> 02:43.280
there's no way to

02:43.280 --> 02:44.400
cross-check all these files,

02:44.400 --> 02:45.740
let alone file them properly.

02:45.740 --> 02:46.670
Time.

02:47.930 --> 02:49.060
Can you

02:49.079 --> 02:51.430
give me a full sentence?

02:51.530 --> 02:54.410
My mentor said
ordinary people might not understand,

02:54.410 --> 02:56.410
but she had all the time in the world.

02:56.810 --> 02:57.930
You mean

02:57.960 --> 03:02.910
your mentor said
she could memorize all of these?

03:03.910 --> 03:05.300
That's impossible.

03:05.580 --> 03:07.670
Even a lifetime wouldn't be enough

03:07.690 --> 03:10.290
for an ordinary person
to memorize all of this.

03:12.600 --> 03:17.900
[Telegraph Office, Branch No. 05]

03:18.000 --> 03:20.200
I knew there was this telegraph office.

03:20.250 --> 03:21.620
No way my memory was off.

03:32.900 --> 03:34.370
Five, four, nine...

03:36.760 --> 03:37.850
Five, four, nine?

03:38.630 --> 03:39.760
Five, four, nine...

03:44.970 --> 03:45.630
Found it?

04:01.250 --> 04:02.560
The first medicinal herb.

04:02.560 --> 04:03.570
Two more to go.

04:03.670 --> 04:04.640
Is this it?

04:07.510 --> 04:08.910
Such an important thing,

04:09.030 --> 04:10.960
a-and it's just kept in a file bag?

04:13.210 --> 04:14.270
Reverse thinking.

04:14.320 --> 04:15.400
The more important something is,

04:15.400 --> 04:16.660
the more it should be kept
in an inconspicuous place.

04:16.660 --> 04:18.740
That way, it's less likely
to attract attention.

04:18.740 --> 04:20.500
T-That's all there is to it?

04:21.220 --> 04:22.620
You think that's simple?

04:23.040 --> 04:25.100
I probably would've thought so once.

04:25.390 --> 04:26.780
But not anymore.

04:31.950 --> 04:34.070
Southern Archives:

04:34.070 --> 04:36.570
Director, one. Administrator, one.

04:36.570 --> 04:37.930
Inspector, one.

04:38.600 --> 04:41.390
In addition, Commissioners,
Vice Commissioners, and others

04:41.390 --> 04:43.860
assigned to patrol
the Nanyang coastal areas

04:43.860 --> 04:44.750
have no fixed number,

04:44.750 --> 04:45.730
as circumstances require.

04:45.730 --> 04:48.350
Upon completion of duty, report back.
Assignments may be terminated at any time.

04:48.350 --> 04:50.480
This is the roster
of your Southern Archives.

04:48.620 --> 04:51.620
[Southern Archives Personnel Roster]

04:50.610 --> 04:52.130
A record of all the staff members.

04:51.640 --> 04:52.730
[Name: Zhang Ruifu] [Appointed as
Commissioner of the Southern Archives]

04:52.930 --> 04:55.180
How come everyone in your Archives

04:55.180 --> 04:56.870
is named Zhang?

04:56.870 --> 04:58.190
Is it a family business?

04:58.190 --> 05:00.450
My mentor said Zhang is a common surname—

05:00.700 --> 05:02.090
it helps us blend in easily

05:02.090 --> 05:03.090
and go unnoticed.

05:03.510 --> 05:06.140
I changed my surname to Zhang
after being taken in.

05:06.140 --> 05:08.570
Maybe the Archives likes to
take in orphans.

05:08.570 --> 05:10.920
Seems like you're
a charitable organization.

05:10.920 --> 05:12.010
And I've noticed

05:12.250 --> 05:15.000
you tend to favor older personnel.

05:12.460 --> 05:14.620
[Name: Zhang Jianbin] [Appointed as
Commissioner of the Southern Archives]

05:14.660 --> 05:16.440
[Name: Zhang Haini] [Appointed as
Commissioner of the Southern Archives]

05:15.030 --> 05:16.770
You really like hiring older staff.

05:16.770 --> 05:17.830
Well, we really do.

05:19.060 --> 05:20.780
Maybe the Zhangs just
tend to live longer.

05:20.780 --> 05:21.100
[Name: Zhang Ruiping] [Appointed as
Commissioner of the Southern Archives]

05:23.030 --> 05:23.890
What are these?

05:25.700 --> 05:29.410
[Name: Zhang Haiqi] [Appointed as Director
of the Southern Archives]

05:25.920 --> 05:28.930
Zhang Haiqi,
Director of the Southern Archives.

05:42.470 --> 05:44.820
[Xiacheng, Late Qing Dynasty]

05:55.350 --> 06:01.830
[Danan Telegraph Office]

05:55.740 --> 05:56.330
Yeah!

05:56.330 --> 05:57.430
Yeah!

05:57.810 --> 05:59.810
Danan Telegraph Office?

06:00.600 --> 06:01.270
Yeah!

06:02.510 --> 06:03.450
Is a "telegraph office"

06:03.450 --> 06:05.300
what Westerners would call a post office?

06:05.080 --> 06:07.430
[Danan Telegraph Office]

06:05.300 --> 06:07.830
I heard Westerners practice
a kind of sorcery.

06:07.830 --> 06:10.410
They can summon the souls of the dead
from their graves

06:10.410 --> 06:12.210
and make them deliver messages.

06:12.300 --> 06:15.010
Their news can travel thousands of miles
in a single day.

06:15.010 --> 06:16.470
How is that even possible?

06:16.740 --> 06:18.380
Witchcraft. It has to be witchcraft.

06:18.380 --> 06:19.370
Yes.

06:19.450 --> 06:20.480
That's because

06:20.480 --> 06:23.910
the telegraph wires are specifically
routed over graveyards.

06:23.910 --> 06:24.830
That's so unlucky.

06:24.030 --> 06:26.640
[Danan Telegraph Office]

06:24.870 --> 06:26.070
Go. Let's leave here.

06:26.180 --> 06:27.240
Let's go, let's go.

06:29.980 --> 06:37.500
[Danan Telegraph Office]

06:33.240 --> 06:33.840
Director,

06:34.450 --> 06:35.690
the soul-summoning stories

06:35.690 --> 06:38.020
have been spreading rapidly around here.

06:38.240 --> 06:40.950
The Southern Archives is being built
underground beneath a busy district.

06:40.950 --> 06:42.480
Some noise is unavoidable.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.700
Having civilians steer clear

06:45.070 --> 06:47.390
actually makes it easier
for us to operate.

06:47.390 --> 06:49.860
Spread a few more stories like that.

06:50.970 --> 06:51.409
Yes.

06:54.460 --> 06:56.490
[Danan Telegraph Office]

07:00.070 --> 07:01.800
Looks like I know nothing about

07:01.800 --> 07:03.260
my mentor or the Archives.

07:09.530 --> 07:10.410
Put it back.

07:14.660 --> 07:16.620
Now that we've found what we came for,

07:16.620 --> 07:17.630
let's hurry

07:18.680 --> 07:19.770
and find a way out.

07:21.450 --> 07:23.510
I've only found the first item I need.

07:23.740 --> 07:24.900
You can leave if you want.

07:24.900 --> 07:25.850
Only one?

07:27.000 --> 07:27.800
That won't do.

07:28.620 --> 07:30.980
According to the land deed,
the Southern Archives

07:30.980 --> 07:32.610
belongs to Haili Bank.

07:32.770 --> 07:34.860
Don't even think about wrecking the place.

07:34.860 --> 07:36.620
Once I've found what I need,

07:36.830 --> 07:37.690
this place is all yours.

07:37.690 --> 07:38.750
Oh, give me a break.

07:39.270 --> 07:41.890
From what I can tell, you don't know much
about the Archives either.

07:41.890 --> 07:43.300
You don't have a say.

07:48.860 --> 07:49.420
Cousin.

07:50.750 --> 07:52.080
Do you smell something?

07:53.630 --> 07:54.740
Yes.

07:55.230 --> 07:57.360
Why is there such a strong moldy smell?

07:57.570 --> 07:58.900
You don't know about it?

08:18.330 --> 08:20.460
Something feels off about this place.

08:20.860 --> 08:21.680
Be careful.

09:48.500 --> 09:54.690
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

09:55.170 --> 09:57.670
[Episode 14]

10:12.720 --> 10:13.540
Be careful.

10:26.170 --> 10:27.790
What exactly happened here?

10:28.810 --> 10:31.340
Looks like it's been abandoned
for a very long time.

10:31.340 --> 10:33.060
There were moles here before.

10:33.240 --> 10:34.770
That's why it was shut down.

10:35.200 --> 10:37.050
And those moles could change their faces.

10:37.050 --> 10:38.220
So whenever we came here,

10:38.220 --> 10:40.050
we had to check each other's faces.

10:40.050 --> 10:40.740
Like this.

10:41.320 --> 10:41.980
Stop it.

10:43.410 --> 10:44.670
Your wound split open.

10:45.630 --> 10:46.130
Your...

10:46.130 --> 10:47.660
Your wound reopened too...

10:54.200 --> 10:55.040
How did...

10:55.340 --> 10:57.510
How did both of our wounds split open?

11:01.640 --> 11:03.960
Do you know about
a certain kind of bat saliva?

11:03.960 --> 11:05.670
Of course I don't!

11:05.820 --> 11:06.960
What should we do now?

11:06.960 --> 11:09.040
It keeps wounds from healing.

11:09.580 --> 11:10.250
I'm guessing

11:10.250 --> 11:11.860
the blades behind that jade gate earlier

11:11.860 --> 11:13.250
were coated with that bat saliva.

11:13.250 --> 11:14.510
Plus, it's warm and humid here,

11:14.510 --> 11:15.770
so our wounds split open.

11:15.770 --> 11:16.890
T-Then what do we do now?

11:16.890 --> 11:18.220
The door here is locked.

11:18.530 --> 11:19.250
Let's go back first.

11:19.250 --> 11:20.810
Okay, okay. Let's go.

11:23.420 --> 11:24.020
Hurry.

11:25.070 --> 11:26.260
Help me, help me.

11:26.850 --> 11:27.420
Hurry.

11:31.440 --> 11:32.460
What's wrong now?

11:34.050 --> 11:35.130
Do you know what a rat trap is?

11:35.130 --> 11:36.250
W-What do you mean?

11:36.750 --> 11:39.080
We are the rats
caught inside it right now.

11:39.200 --> 11:39.950
What should we do?

11:39.950 --> 11:40.770
Don't panic.

11:41.150 --> 11:42.680
I'll figure something out.

11:45.480 --> 11:46.470
Hurry up.

11:48.010 --> 11:48.880
Well?

11:49.120 --> 11:50.250
Can you decipher it?

11:50.480 --> 11:51.370
Can you?

11:51.370 --> 11:52.220
Can you decipher it?

11:52.220 --> 11:52.780
Be quiet.

11:52.910 --> 11:53.670
Isn't this the answer your buddy

11:53.670 --> 11:55.210
deliberately left for you?

11:55.240 --> 11:56.600
How can you still not figure it out?

11:56.600 --> 11:57.980
Were you two even on the same wavelength?

11:57.980 --> 11:59.040
I said, be quiet!

11:59.580 --> 12:01.480
I don't mean to, but I'm scared!

12:01.820 --> 12:02.740
What should we do now?

12:02.740 --> 12:04.600
I'm too scared to shut up.

12:15.350 --> 12:16.410
What's happening?

12:16.410 --> 12:17.470
What's that?

12:23.080 --> 12:23.900
What's that?

12:26.740 --> 12:28.200
Plague, what should we do?

12:35.300 --> 12:37.130
There must be
some special mechanism up there

12:37.130 --> 12:38.440
that creates a kind of

12:38.440 --> 12:40.510
negative-pressure vacuum in this space.

12:40.510 --> 12:42.710
Just like drawing blood with a syringe.

12:43.340 --> 12:44.570
I tried stabbing it with my knife.

12:44.570 --> 12:45.830
The surface is too hard

12:46.130 --> 12:47.290
to break through.

12:47.440 --> 12:48.520
So,

12:48.600 --> 12:50.350
the previous trap and this one

12:50.390 --> 12:51.520
are the same trap.

12:51.700 --> 12:53.270
The wounds we got earlier

12:53.270 --> 12:55.730
are meant to bleed us to death
in here, right?

12:56.410 --> 12:57.740
Very ingenious, right?

12:57.750 --> 12:58.960
As expected of Shrimpie.

12:58.960 --> 13:00.200
Are you insane?

13:00.410 --> 13:02.500
At a time like this,
you're still praising him?

13:02.500 --> 13:04.080
Think of a way out!

13:04.080 --> 13:06.390
Your friend is going to get us killed.

13:08.080 --> 13:09.610
He used double encryption.

13:09.750 --> 13:11.390
The first layer is two-square cipher.

13:11.390 --> 13:12.780
As for the second layer...

13:12.780 --> 13:14.640
I don't know which system he used.

13:15.210 --> 13:16.680
Quickly think of a way out.

13:17.030 --> 13:17.770
Did he

13:18.270 --> 13:20.200
say anything special

13:20.480 --> 13:21.250
or mention

13:21.370 --> 13:22.200
any little...

13:22.480 --> 13:23.510
little habits?

13:23.820 --> 13:24.420
Little...

13:25.100 --> 13:25.700
Little...

13:28.270 --> 13:29.670
If I die,

13:30.280 --> 13:31.420
who will save you?

13:37.770 --> 13:40.300
Were we really that bad
at reading each other?

13:46.780 --> 13:48.860
Our hideout for dividing the loot
is so well concealed.

13:48.860 --> 13:50.120
How did this cop know?

13:50.390 --> 13:52.910
You little brat, who sent you?

13:55.080 --> 13:56.270
Won't talk, huh?

13:56.940 --> 13:57.850
Go to hell!

14:00.510 --> 14:01.600
Police!

14:02.390 --> 14:03.840
You're surrounded!

14:03.840 --> 14:05.650
Drop your weapons within one minute,

14:05.650 --> 14:07.250
and we will spare your lives.

14:11.250 --> 14:12.510
Didn't I tell you to leave first?

14:12.510 --> 14:13.650
No one's leaving!

14:44.480 --> 14:45.340
Where are they?

14:45.360 --> 14:47.070
Find them! Don't let them get away!

14:47.070 --> 14:47.480
Yes, boss!

14:47.480 --> 14:47.840
Yes!

14:48.000 --> 14:49.030
Check over there!

14:49.340 --> 14:50.540
Why did you come back?

14:50.820 --> 14:51.790
Did you forget the rules?

14:51.790 --> 14:53.340
If I hadn't, you'd be dead.

14:56.510 --> 14:57.630
And coming back actually helped?

14:57.630 --> 14:58.460
I'd say it helped quite a bit.

14:58.460 --> 14:59.460
Check over there.

14:59.570 --> 15:00.180
Yes.

15:00.630 --> 15:02.090
Did you bring any weapons?

15:14.940 --> 15:15.580
Come at me!

16:33.950 --> 16:34.910
Don't let him get away!

16:34.910 --> 16:35.620
After him!

17:19.400 --> 17:20.220
You really think our secret code

17:20.220 --> 17:21.880
would be that easy to imitate?

17:22.010 --> 17:23.240
What secret code?

17:41.740 --> 17:43.070
You prepared the crate?

17:45.420 --> 17:47.640
How could you have
calculated everything so precisely?

17:47.640 --> 17:49.240
If you ever get into trouble,

17:49.270 --> 17:50.530
take three steps back.

17:50.770 --> 17:54.030
I'll be right behind you
to ensure you have a fallback plan.

17:56.050 --> 17:58.290
The second layer of code on this banknote

17:58.290 --> 17:59.460
uses a skip-pattern cipher.

17:59.460 --> 18:03.050
First, replace each letter with the one
three places earlier in the alphabet,

18:03.050 --> 18:05.200
then decode it with the two-square cipher.

18:05.200 --> 18:05.960
D,

18:06.740 --> 18:07.460
R,

18:08.500 --> 18:09.270
Y.

18:11.290 --> 18:12.860
Drying file...

18:54.760 --> 18:55.650
What's wrong?

18:56.250 --> 18:56.890
Cousin,

18:57.790 --> 18:58.720
the door is open.

19:01.000 --> 19:01.840
I'm not dead?

19:02.570 --> 19:03.340
Plague,

19:03.400 --> 19:04.560
help me, help me.

19:24.720 --> 19:26.850
I've found the second medicinal herb.

19:27.700 --> 19:28.570
One more left.

19:47.440 --> 19:48.200
Sir,

19:48.220 --> 19:49.680
we found something. Look!

20:00.850 --> 20:02.770
An underground passage again.

20:02.770 --> 20:04.500
You have committed grave sins.

20:08.130 --> 20:09.690
If you can make it out alive,

20:09.910 --> 20:11.040
you'll be pardoned.

20:11.090 --> 20:12.050
I'll let you go.

20:13.570 --> 20:15.090
But in all this time,

20:15.350 --> 20:16.460
no one has ever

20:16.460 --> 20:18.000
come out of there alive.

22:26.180 --> 22:27.810
Blow it open.

22:28.400 --> 22:28.980
Yes, sir!

22:53.370 --> 22:54.230
What happened?

22:55.920 --> 22:57.110
You did pretty well back there.

22:57.110 --> 23:00.040
For an ordinary person,
that was pretty impressive.

23:00.050 --> 23:02.580
So not dying is considered
a success now, huh?

23:02.680 --> 23:04.250
If it keeps going like this,

23:04.770 --> 23:06.370
I might not be able to keep up.

23:06.480 --> 23:07.800
You chose this path yourself.

23:07.800 --> 23:08.930
What else can you do?

23:11.470 --> 23:12.690
What's this?

23:14.070 --> 23:15.400
This is my compass.

23:17.530 --> 23:17.980
Sometimes,

23:17.980 --> 23:20.040
I really admire this friend of yours.

23:20.270 --> 23:21.930
Is all this really necessary?

23:22.220 --> 23:25.030
Did he have to make the clues
this complicated?

23:30.130 --> 23:30.760
Cousin,

23:31.270 --> 23:32.720
you seem particularly interested

23:32.720 --> 23:33.850
in our Archives.

23:34.240 --> 23:36.000
We happen to be short-handed recently.

23:36.000 --> 23:37.730
Ever thought about joining us?

23:41.870 --> 23:43.730
I should just keep things simple.

23:44.400 --> 23:45.650
Living an ordinary life

23:45.650 --> 23:46.850
is good enough for me.

23:58.040 --> 23:59.700
Always forgetting things...

24:01.180 --> 24:02.000
The clue...

24:03.050 --> 24:03.840
Clue...

24:05.160 --> 24:05.950
Master...

24:06.790 --> 24:07.800
Our mentor?

24:09.270 --> 24:10.400
What does this mean?

24:15.380 --> 24:16.640
This cave is spacious.

24:17.010 --> 24:18.270
There's much more air.

24:20.310 --> 24:21.110
Here, Plague.

24:21.750 --> 24:22.570
Your clue.

24:22.940 --> 24:23.580
What clue?

24:23.740 --> 24:24.310
Here.

24:57.440 --> 24:58.500
You wanna study it?

24:58.720 --> 24:59.290
Okay.

25:17.200 --> 25:18.500
So what's drawn on here

25:19.160 --> 25:20.550
are these cracks.

25:23.420 --> 25:25.290
[Double Clouds]

25:24.460 --> 25:26.200
Isn't "Double Clouds" the crack

25:26.200 --> 25:27.590
we just walked through?

25:27.130 --> 25:27.970
[Double Clouds]

25:28.510 --> 25:30.440
In ancient usage,
"double clouds" means eyes.

25:30.440 --> 25:31.700
So when we crawled through there,

25:31.700 --> 25:34.500
we had to keep our eyes wide open
without blinking.

25:36.830 --> 25:38.260
So these names

25:38.700 --> 25:40.940
describe the characteristics
of each passage.

25:40.940 --> 25:42.200
What about these?

25:57.680 --> 25:59.680
This one's called "Broken Dragon."

26:03.300 --> 26:04.750
[Ah Xiang]

26:08.530 --> 26:10.220
Now, this one is quite something.

26:10.220 --> 26:11.220
This one is called

26:11.400 --> 26:12.140
"Ah Xiang."

26:13.090 --> 26:13.830
Broken Dragon, Ah Xiang...

26:13.830 --> 26:15.680
Why do those names sound so rustic?

26:15.680 --> 26:16.290
Alright.

26:16.420 --> 26:18.080
Never mind if they're rustic.

26:18.350 --> 26:20.080
Well, which one should we take?

26:20.640 --> 26:22.700
Which one do you think we should take?

26:28.920 --> 26:29.740
Ah Xiang.

26:46.500 --> 26:47.010
Wait,

26:47.010 --> 26:47.720
why?

26:48.440 --> 26:49.970
How did you figure that out?

26:51.650 --> 26:52.210
Plague?

26:52.480 --> 26:53.010
Plague!

26:54.050 --> 26:56.780
How did you know
Broken Dragon was the right path?

26:57.290 --> 26:59.550
Because "Broken Dragon" sounds cooler.

27:00.720 --> 27:01.810
Fine, fine.

27:10.700 --> 27:12.360
Being cool does have its uses.

27:15.850 --> 27:16.710
Broken Dragon?

27:19.510 --> 27:20.960
What does that even mean?

27:25.920 --> 27:26.640
Plague,

27:27.880 --> 27:29.540
there's writing carved here.

27:38.680 --> 27:42.050
"Year 25, abnormal movements
were detected beneath Xiacheng.

27:42.050 --> 27:44.220
The Director of the Southern Archives

27:44.220 --> 27:45.810
followed the underground fissures downward

27:45.810 --> 27:47.610
and discovered the Underworld.

27:47.740 --> 27:50.270
Using feng shui
to suppress the dragon vein.

27:51.140 --> 27:53.500
As long as the underground dragon vein
of Xiacheng remains,

27:53.500 --> 27:55.160
seawater cannot flood inward,

27:55.160 --> 27:58.380
and the secret of the underground
remains hidden from the world.

27:58.380 --> 28:01.400
The Southern Archives was
subsequently established here

28:01.400 --> 28:03.460
to oversee all affairs of the South."

28:04.270 --> 28:06.850
We should be at
the very bottom boundary marker

28:06.850 --> 28:08.510
of the Southern Archives now.

28:13.530 --> 28:16.200
Behind this should be
the suppressed Underworld.

28:16.200 --> 28:17.380
The Underworld?

28:18.290 --> 28:20.030
Legend has it that the Archives
was built so deep

28:20.030 --> 28:22.010
in order to suppress
something underground.

28:22.010 --> 28:24.680
Then what does
"the secret of the underground" mean?

28:24.680 --> 28:26.240
The secret inside is crucial

28:26.240 --> 28:27.330
and must never be revealed.

28:27.330 --> 28:30.610
That's why they used two layers
of Dragon-Sealing Stones, inside and out,

28:30.610 --> 28:31.530
to keep it suppressed.

28:31.530 --> 28:33.380
Since it's a secret,

28:33.400 --> 28:35.030
why carve it onto a stone monument?

28:35.030 --> 28:36.560
And spell it out so clearly?

28:37.570 --> 28:38.600
It's a warning

28:39.680 --> 28:42.750
to tell people what's inside is
even more dangerous than what's outside.

28:42.750 --> 28:45.150
Looks like what I'm looking for
is in there.

28:47.480 --> 28:48.660
Is this a switch?

28:49.770 --> 28:50.770
It's really ugly.

29:43.590 --> 29:44.320
Sir.

29:47.520 --> 29:49.240
What's the situation down there?

29:49.240 --> 29:50.710
Three Maxim guns.

29:51.070 --> 29:52.090
Maxim guns?

29:53.670 --> 29:54.900
What do we do now, sir?

29:55.550 --> 29:58.350
Zhang Haiqi really
has everything planned out.

29:59.140 --> 30:01.730
She's using the Maxim machine guns

30:01.940 --> 30:03.180
to buy time

30:03.770 --> 30:06.570
until reinforcements arrive
from the consulate.

30:15.640 --> 30:16.720
But the Commander said

30:16.720 --> 30:17.790
that without his permission,

30:17.790 --> 30:19.190
we absolutely cannot...

30:20.380 --> 30:20.940
Sir...

30:21.480 --> 30:23.240
Go back and get it.

30:41.750 --> 30:43.770
After that gunfire, no one was left.

30:43.770 --> 30:44.680
If they can't figure out a way,

30:44.680 --> 30:46.480
they'll have to escape!

30:46.500 --> 30:47.690
Come on, boys!

30:48.070 --> 30:48.960
Pack up

30:48.960 --> 30:49.810
all these treasures!

30:49.810 --> 30:51.470
There's a share for everyone!

30:54.940 --> 30:56.010
Miss Dong,

30:56.090 --> 30:57.500
you really dug deep
into your pockets this time.

30:57.500 --> 30:58.760
I'd say we're even now.

30:58.790 --> 31:00.330
It's been a pleasure working with you.

31:00.330 --> 31:01.750
Don't celebrate too soon.

31:01.750 --> 31:04.010
Lu Junxiang won't just give up like that.

31:05.830 --> 31:08.200
Is that so? My Maxim guns might

31:08.200 --> 31:10.060
have something to say about that.

31:59.510 --> 32:01.440
I've put up with you for a long time.

32:01.570 --> 32:02.980
When did you find out?

32:03.570 --> 32:05.950
I can smell blood on people.

32:06.220 --> 32:07.480
You've killed people,

32:07.510 --> 32:09.050
but He Jianxi hasn't.

32:09.050 --> 32:10.310
Just based on that?

32:10.960 --> 32:12.220
Are you a dog?

32:13.460 --> 32:15.660
Mostly because your acting was terrible.

32:15.660 --> 32:17.640
He Jianxi has
an unusually keen sense of smell.

32:17.640 --> 32:19.510
But at the Bronze Ball Mechanism,

32:19.510 --> 32:21.880
you actually smelled that gunpowder
later than I did.

32:21.880 --> 32:23.310
Then forget looking for a key.

32:23.310 --> 32:25.170
Let's just break the door open.

32:27.510 --> 32:28.970
There's a smell of sulfur,

32:29.330 --> 32:31.330
so there must be explosives inside.

32:32.340 --> 32:33.280
It really is.

32:33.510 --> 32:34.320
That's when I knew

32:34.320 --> 32:35.840
you weren't He Jianxi.

32:36.480 --> 32:39.810
And the most ridiculous part is
that you somehow got taller.

32:51.070 --> 32:52.310
Then why

32:53.090 --> 32:54.820
didn't you act on it at the time?

32:55.180 --> 32:56.740
If I'd killed you then,

32:56.940 --> 32:59.180
who would've kept me entertained
along the way?

32:59.180 --> 33:00.350
I'd have been bored to death.

33:00.350 --> 33:01.060
Besides,

33:01.440 --> 33:02.050
I wasn't sure

33:02.050 --> 33:03.910
whether you were sent by my mentor

33:04.000 --> 33:05.860
or by the enemies of the Archives.

33:06.110 --> 33:07.230
After all, you did save me once

33:07.230 --> 33:08.760
and got the medicine for me.

33:09.720 --> 33:10.890
I promised my mentor

33:11.700 --> 33:13.500
I'd break this bad habit of mine.

33:19.590 --> 33:21.020
So you're saying

33:22.030 --> 33:24.090
you were risking your life to test me?

33:25.240 --> 33:27.570
Is everyone from the Archives this crazy?

33:28.220 --> 33:29.280
Where is my cousin?

33:29.400 --> 33:30.300
He's fine.

33:34.140 --> 33:34.920
That's good.

33:36.980 --> 33:38.440
Since you've attacked me,

33:39.100 --> 33:41.430
you definitely weren't sent by my mentor.

33:42.190 --> 33:43.040
So now...

33:44.790 --> 33:45.660
you can die.

34:00.180 --> 34:01.500
You spy,

34:01.500 --> 34:02.650
drop the act.

34:03.050 --> 34:04.510
Where did those banknotes come from?

34:04.510 --> 34:05.570
What are you trying to get inside there?

34:05.570 --> 34:06.550
You bastard,

34:06.550 --> 34:09.280
how dare you pretend to be
a good guy in front of me?

36:08.070 --> 36:09.600
Sir, no sign of Zhang Haiqi.

36:11.870 --> 36:13.680
What a pity.

36:24.340 --> 36:26.180
Sir! Sir!

36:26.480 --> 36:27.470
Bad news, sir!

36:28.570 --> 36:30.070
The outer underground structure
has completely collapsed!

36:30.070 --> 36:31.800
Huge amounts of seawater are pouring in!

36:31.800 --> 36:32.960
If we don't leave now,

36:32.960 --> 36:34.420
we'll all drown down here!

36:40.210 --> 36:42.730
Keep pursuing Zhang Haiqi!

36:42.730 --> 36:43.560
Yes, sir!

36:47.760 --> 36:50.290
Zhang Hailou,
you've finally made it inside.

36:50.480 --> 36:51.900
But you're out of time.

36:52.630 --> 36:53.970
The Archives is about to be flooded.
